  "transcript": {
    "language": "en",
    "coverage_ratio": 0.98,
    "text": "Claude Fable 5.2 is out, and if you're on a pro or team plan, it's included at no extra cost until November 16th. | So, this is how we'd use that week. | Take this first. Fable is the most powerful Claude you can use. | The same brain as Mythos with safety filters on top, and this version is up to 30% faster and 20% cheaper on the API than the last one. | Now, what to use it for? | Anthropic itself says to start your normal day on Opus 5.5 and bring in Fable for the hardest open-ended work, | like moving a big code base over to something new, | a tough math or engineering problem, | or a job where it runs a team of agents for hours. | It can even be the boss | and hand the easy parts to smaller models. | For quick emails and small questions, it's a waste | because Fable eats through your limit faster than any other Claude. | To switch, in the Claude app, | open the model picker and choose Fable 5.2, | and your default stays the same. | In Claude code, update it first, type slash model, | pick Fable, and press the S key instead of enter | so it's only for that session | and doesn't become your default without you noticing. | On Pro, you get up to half your weekly limit on Fable until November 16th, plus one free | reset if you run out. | And after that, it runs on usage credits. | So pick the one problem you gave up on, the hardest thing on your list, and hand it to | Fable this week."
